  "comments": "The standard weight of these coins was 8/11 troy ounce (349.1 grains).<br /><br />\r\nThis particular coin was not included in demonetization legislation when decimalisation was introduced in 1971. It has been confirmed by the Royal Mint that the coin remains legal tender, having been remonetized with a value of 20 pence.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse die varieties:</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#3922</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1887 only)</span> Roman I in date;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#3923</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1887-90)</span> Arabic 1 in date;<br /><br />\r\nThe 1887 mintage data includes both die varieties.",
